1
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:25,080
-You're so pretty.
-Mm-hm.

2
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,040
Who's that woman?

3
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:36,280
WAREHOUSE
MINI FARM FAIR

4
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:38,480
Rut, what is this?

5
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,360
Ms. Ming?

6
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,600
Who's this? You know her?

7
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,200
Ms. Ming is Mr. Chettha's daughter.

8
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,360
So…

9
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:01,400
-You and she are--
-Together.

10
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:03,960
Together?

11
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:08,919
You just broke up with me yesterday.
Since when did you start seeing her?

12
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,160
Didn't you break up with her ages ago?

13
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:16,120
So you did cheat on me first.

14
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:17,880
I cheated on you?

15
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:22,080
You're the one two-timing me with Din.

16
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:25,440
I told you there was nothing
between Din and me!

17
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,720
-Ask anybody.
-Yeah.

18
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,240
He's teaching her about buffaloes.

19
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,880
Shut up, Ob! Stop defending her!

20
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:34,800
I'm a man, too.
I know the way he looks at her.

21
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,440
You like my girl, don't you?

22
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:44,120
I know you've always
been waiting for your chance.

23
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,240
I bet you're glad we broke up!

24
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,320
-That's enough, Rut!
-Did I hit a nerve?

25
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,360
-Did I? Just say it!
-Rut, enough already!

26
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:53,560
Or are you not into her at all? Tell me?

27
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:55,200
-Rut!
-Yeah.

28
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,000
I like Auem.

29
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,280
But she doesn't feel the same way.

30
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,240
She never cheated on you or two-timed you.

31
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,320
I'm actually glad

32
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:12,480
that Auem's finally free
from a pathetic leech like you.

33
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:16,960
-Who did you call a leech, buffalo boy?
-No, Rut!

34
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,480
-Rut, no!
-Who?

35
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:20,040
-Say it!
-You are!

36
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:21,640
You think I don't know?

37
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:25,040
You dated Auem for her family's money.

38
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:29,200
But as soon as Uncle Yod died,
you ghosted her.

39
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:32,400
Have you ever thought
about what she's going through?

40
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,000
Go be with her then.

41
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:39,920
She's all yours.

42
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:45,240
-Din! Enough. Please stop!
-You hit me! Bring it on, Rut!

43
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:48,280
-Rut, no!
-Let go of me! Let go!

44
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,080
Let's go, Ms. Ming.

45
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,760
These scumbags don't deserve our time.

46
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:01,640
Wait, Rut.

47
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,280
-Rut, wait!
-Auem.

48
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:06,960
What more do you want?

49
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:11,640
Give me back all the gold
I've saved up with you.

50
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:14,200
What gold, Rut?

51
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:19,600
The gold Rut and I have saved
for our wedding.

52
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,800
Five baht of gold.

53
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:28,880
When did we do that?
You're talking nonsense.

54
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,240
I transferred you the money every month.

55
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:35,280
Here. The latest bank transfer receipt
from two months ago.

56
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:39,000
TRANSFER SUCCESSFUL
3,000 BAHT

57
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,360
And you're gonna give me all the gold

58
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:47,000
since you broke your promise.

59
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:54,080
SAVING GOLD, BUILDING LOVE
FOR AUEM AND RUT'S FUTURE

60
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:58,640
What's the problem?

61
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,880
No gold to give her?

62
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,760
It's not that.

63
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:08,240
I'm at work.
I'll bring it to you after my shift.

64
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:11,680
It's okay. I can tell Mr. Chettha
that you're going home to get the gold.

65
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,080
Wait, Auem! Don't!

66
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,000
Why?

67
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,320
Was Din right? You don't have
the gold anymore, do you?

68
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,400
Tell me!

69
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,200
No.

70
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:32,480
I don't.

71
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,400
I sold all of it.

72
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:38,080
You're a real piece of work, Rut.

73
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:41,320
No wonder you wanted to break up
with her so badly.

74
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,600
Give me back all my money.

75
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:49,960
You have until Monday.
If I don't get it back by then,

76
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:54,720
Mr. Chettha will know about this.
And I'll tell everyone here at the store

77
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:58,240
that his daughter took my boyfriend.

78
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,440
Five baht of gold, right?

79
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:08,120
I'll give you 300,000.

80
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,440
Your bank details?

81
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:28,080
And keep your mouth shut after this.
Don't you say anything to my dad.

82
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,040
And if you're not done,

83
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,760
then start looking for a new job.

84
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:41,040
TRANSFER SUCCESSFUL
300,000 BAHT

85
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:55,280
ANIMAL FEED STORE

86
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:58,200
Step right up! Here at Chettha Kaset Farm,

87
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:00,560
we offer a wide range of animal feed.

88
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:03,080
If you want to bulk up your buffaloes,

89
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:07,360
I recommend the 16%
and 21% protein formulas.

90
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:12,120
I'll show you how to make a feed mix
that I make for Hom Ngern.

91
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:20,040
For this formula, I use around
seven pounds of 16% protein feed,

92
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,800
around two pounds of 21% protein feed,

93
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:26,320
roughly another two and a half pounds
of feed mix from our own farm,

94
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:29,840
one bucket of ground corn,
and half a bucket of soybean meal.

95
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:47,560
If you're interested,
please come in and take a look.

96
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,520
We have a lot of promotions going on.

97
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:50,920
Please come in.

98
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:59,200
WAREHOUSE
MINI FARM FAIR

99
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,880
-Dad.
-Hmm?

100
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,360
What is it, dear?

101
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,600
-You've got to fire Auemdao.
-What?

102
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:14,400
Why would I do that?

103
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,680
Did she do something?

104
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:19,160
I just don't like her.

105
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:20,880
Ming.

106
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:25,080
You can't make me fire my staff
just because you don't like her.

107
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:27,920
Auemdao just started around a week ago,

108
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,720
but she's doing great.

109
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:33,120
Her marketing plans
are also pretty interesting.

110
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,240
I can't fire her.

111
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:47,840
Come on in.

112
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,120
MAE SA-ANG
DELICIOUS ASSORTED DISHES

113
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:02,200
Okay, all done.

114
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:03,680
All done!

115
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:07,240
All done? Come skewer the meatballs then.

116
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:10,160
Come on.

117
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,400
Aren't you gonna give me a break?

118
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:15,360
I've been here since 5 a.m.
I prepared everything.

119
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:19,080
Stir-fry vegetables,
clear soup, steamed rice.

120
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:21,240
I did everything.
Even the Chinese-spiced eggs!

121
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,680
My legs are aching from all this standing.

122
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,000
-Aching?
-Yeah.

123
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,240
-You're tired?
-Yeah.

124
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:28,480
Go get Orn to help us then.

125
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,040
It's almost lunch break.

126
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,000
Never mind.

127
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:35,800
I can work to pay off the debt myself.
No need to bother her.

128
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:38,200
Wow, you sure are spoiling her.

129
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,560
That's enough. Be quiet.

130
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:50,640
Wait, these meatballs are mostly flour.
You're really selling these to kids?

131
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:55,240
These assorted dishes take up all my time.

132
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:57,720
It's easier to buy and resell meatballs.

133
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,160
What if I make the meatballs myself?

134
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:09,600
If we make a big profit,
will you let me keep all of it?

135
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:12,360
If that's really the case,

136
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:14,880
you can keep it all.

137
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:17,840
-You mean it?
-Yeah.

138
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:34,880
-Meatballs are here, kids!
-Freshly made, too. See all that steam?

139
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,920
Wow, look at the steam!
They're fresh and hot.

140
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:38,840
Here.

141
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,240
-Okay.
-What do you think?

142
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,880
-Smells good, no?
-Very.

143
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:45,120
-Freshly made meatballs.
-Freshly made.

144
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,720
-Which dipping sauce?
-Seafood.

145
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,320
Seafood? Okay.

146
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,200
-Here you go.
-How much?

147
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:51,160
Twenty baht, sweetie.

148
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,680
-Here you go.
-Here, right here.

149
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,480
-Which sauce, handsome?
-This one.

150
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,480
-Here.
-How much?

151
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:59,480
-Twenty.
-Here you go. Have some extra balls.

152
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:01,920
Wow, they're delicious!

153
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,480
-Will you make these every day?
-Ooh, really?

154
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:08,120
If you keep saying they're that good,
I'll make them every day.

155
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,720
Our dipping sauces are good too.
Which one do you like?

156
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,240
Chili sauce. It's nice and spicy.

157
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:16,720
-The seafood sauce is even better.
-Yeah.

158
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,320
Well, come eat them every day then.

159
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,840
-That'll keep her going.
-That's right.

160
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:23,520
-Next. What can I get you?
-Come, come.

161
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:27,560
Dang, your business is booming.
I'm jealous.

162
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:30,440
You said something, Jim?

163
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,640
Nothing. I was just trying
to get some buyers.

164
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,360
Yes, dear? You want some spicy salad?

165
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,760
Yummy spicy salad.

166
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,120
Right this way, kiddos.

167
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,960
-Dipping sauce too.
-Thanks.

168
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:46,040
And you? Oh.

169
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,000
Seafood sauce.

170
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:50,200
-The skewer stick's right here.
-Dipping sauce for you?

171
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,760
Let's go mess with her.

172
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:12,960
Orn.

173
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:17,520
You're eating at the canteen?
I thought you'd order sushi from the mall.

174
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:20,320
The restaurant's closed. I couldn't order.

175
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:22,640
Oh.

176
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:39,720
Ning, Orn, Monster Amulet just released

177
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,520
their official merch prices.

178
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:45,360
Wow.

179
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:48,360
-How much for the whole set?
-Five thousand.

180
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,160
It comes with a hat, scarf, shirt,

181
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:53,080
bag, keychain,

182
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:55,120
socks, and a plushie!

183
00:12:57,200 --> 00:13:00,000
Preorder starts this Saturday.
I'll take care of it.

184
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:03,360
Merch pickup's at the concert venue.
One for you, Ning?

185
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,400
And you, Orn?

186
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:11,920
Maybe you don't have enough?
Your mom even has to sell meatballs, no?

187
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,760
Oh yeah. When we were buying
the concert tickets,

188
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:18,640
you took days transferring us the money.

189
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,280
It's okay if you don't have enough.

190
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,680
Ningning and I will just go ahead
and get the merch.

191
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:29,840
Give me two, Maysa.

192
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:33,040
I'll use one at the concert
and keep the other one.

193
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:55,080
I threw in some organic calcium
for you to try too.

194
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:59,040
It'll help your buffaloes look their best
and enhance their build.

195
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,240
-Here you go. We're here until Sunday.
-Thank you.

196
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,480
Come see us anytime.

197
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:04,040
-Sure, thanks.
-Thank you.

198
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,080
Auem.

199
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:27,840
I already took Hom Ngern to the trailer.
Rung and Ob are watching her.

200
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:29,960
Need a hand?

201
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:35,040
Just covering up the booth, really.

202
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:01,360
Yeah! I like Auem.

203
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,520
But she doesn't feel the same way.

204
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,000
Wait! One sec, Auem.

205
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:15,440
Uh…

206
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,960
When I said I like you,

207
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:20,800
I meant it.

208
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,960
But I know that you don't see me that way.

209
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:29,360
Now that I've told you,
I don't want to just let it go.

210
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,840
In your eyes,

211
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:37,400
I might be just a buffalo farmer.

212
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:43,880
But I'm gonna show you
that this buffalo guy…

213
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,560
can really take care of you.

214
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:12,040
NOW IN SERVICE
AYUTTHAYA - BANGKOK MINIBUS

215
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,040
NEW C
2 NEW MESSAGES

216
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:34,960
943 FOLLOWERS. 32 POSTS
YOU FOLLOW EACH OTHER ON INSTAGRAM

217
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:38,320
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I'd like to pre-order these.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">3,600 baht, right?</font></font></i>

218
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">That's right.</font></font></i>

219
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:47,360
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">It'll take seven to ten days to arrive.</font></font></i>

